<title>UK: KfW sets 200 million mark 10-year structured bond. [CORRECTED 11:00 GMT]</title>
<headline>KfW sets 200 million mark 10-year structured bond. [CORRECTED 11:00 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Societe Generale and Bayerische Landesbank.</p>
<p> BORROWER   KREDITANSTALT FUER WIEDERAUFBAU (KFW)</p>
<p> AMT    200 MLN DEM   COUPON   **4.7	 MATURITY    19.MAR.07</p>
<p> TYPE   STRUCTURED    ISS PRICE  102.475   PAY DATE    19.MAR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.5	 LISTING    FFT	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> NOTES    **IN YEAR ONE, THEN 80 PCT OF CONSTANT MATURITY</p>
<p>	    RATE, CAP OF 7.75 PCT (corrects from 7.5 pct), FLOOR OF 4.0 PCT</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  AAA/AAA   MGT/UND    0.325     SELL CONC   2.175</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    GERMAN    HOME CTRY  GERMANY   TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
